From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:43:01 +0100
Subject: Fix: avoid a race in Poppler's colour setup before comparing in
 parallel

The first time Poppler processes a page it creates two global colour
profiles, GfxState::sRGBProfile and GfxXYZ2DisplayTransforms::XYZProfile,
in the GfxState constructor without any locking (poppler 26.07,
GfxState.cc).  Threads doing that at the same moment each assign the
global and free each other's profile, even with separate documents: a
test program in which 16 threads, each with its own Poppler::Document,
call textList() on their first page at once crashes (SIGSEGV, or SIGABRT
from a double free in cmsCloseProfile) in 12 runs out of 100.  Debian's
OpenMP-based diffpdf hits this comparing two 140-page files.

disparPDF's workers start staggered enough that I could not make it
crash, but nothing guarantees that, so comparePagesInParallel() now
processes one page before starting the workers; after that the profiles
are only read.  The same test program with this warm-up: 0 crashes in
100 runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
---
 pagecompare.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pagecompare.cpp b/pagecompare.cpp
index 958ddb8..038fe4b 100644
--- a/pagecompare.cpp
+++ b/pagecompare.cpp
@@ -129,6 +129,17 @@ QVector<PagePairResult> comparePagesInParallel(
         }
     };
 
+    // The first time Poppler processes a page it creates some global colour
+    // profiles, without locking (GfxState::sRGBProfile and
+    // GfxXYZ2DisplayTransforms::XYZProfile).  Workers doing that at once
+    // can free each other's profile and crash, so process one page here
+    // before they start.
+    if (total > 0) {
+        const PdfPage page = pdf1->page(pages1.at(0));
+        if (page)
+            page->textList();
+    }
+
     int wanted = QThread::idealThreadCount();
     if (options.maxWorkers > 0)
         wanted = qMin(wanted, options.maxWorkers);
